  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prevention, protection and assistance to vulnerable survivors of human trafficking in Ukraine, 24-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Next phase of UKR010. Anti-trafficking project led by Caritas Ukraine national office (Safe Migration and Anti-trafficking Department) with 7 regional Caritas organizations: Kyiv (covering Kyiv, Chernihiv, Vinnytsia, Cherkasy, Zhytomyr), Odesa, Ivano-Frankivsk, Lviv, Ternopil, Chernivtsi, and Khmelnytskyi regions.
    
The project goal is to reduce human trafficking by prevention, raising awareness and identification of survivors among the most vulnerable population of Ukraine and provision comprehensive reintegration assistance.
The objectives are:
1. Prevention of human trafficking, raising awareness and advocacy.
2. Proactive screening and identification of the survivors among the vulnerable population. 
3. Comprehensive assistance to the survivors and their family members.
4. Capacity building, knowledge and experience sharing in counter trafficking within stakeholders (both internal &#x2013; Caritas stakeholders, and external &#x2013; subjects of the national referral mechanism).</narrative>
  </description>
